 "market": "As of mid-August 2026, US markets are just off record highs: the S&P 500 hit a fresh all-time high above 7,800 (intraday 7,814; record close ~7,799) on cooling inflation and strong earnings, then eased to ~7,703-7,745, with the Nasdaq near 26,645 — a mild pullback after a strong rally. AI/semiconductor tone is choppy: a late-July selloff wiped over $1T from chip stocks (SMH -9.5% in a month) on fears AI capex is peaking, though analysts frame it as repricing, not demand weakness; Q2 earnings confirm accelerating AI capex and record semi sales (+104% YoY in May). Macro: July CPI rose 0.1% m/m (3.4% y/y); Fed held rates at 3.5%-3.75% in a divided 9-3 vote; new Fed Chair Kevin Warsh's first Jackson Hole speech (Aug 27-29) is the key upcoming catalyst.",
